[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. The page is plain HTML, so I used the browser's built-in [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m
  inside a [38;5;153m<label>[39m and didn't need any JavaScript.

  - [1mOn/off state:[0m the browser handles it. Clicking the box or the text next to it toggles the item.
  - [1mDone styling:[0m a few lines of CSS put a line through checked items and grey them out.
  - [1mExample item:[0m there's one placeholder, "Example task", inside [38;5;153m<main>[39m. To add more, copy the [38;5;153m<label [39m
    [38;5;153mclass="task">…</label>[39m block.

  I haven't opened it in a browser. Ticked items also don't stay ticked after a page reload, which would need a few
  lines of JavaScript to save them; I can add that if you want.

